# Ambient / cinema video

The homepage aerial clip should feel absolutely high end on most devices and connections used by the intended audience (people who can afford to rent a house in the baglio).

For all other audiences and circumstances (like low bandwidth) it should gracefully degrade.

## Premium path (default)

- Gate hero (portone still) → aerial video when the cinema stage enters view (`IntersectionObserver`, `ready` on `AmbientVideo`).
- Desktop landscape: sticky pin, scroll-driven Chi siamo card over the final frame.
- Poster (`poster`) visible until playback; `fetchpriority` on gate, lazy on video.
- One `720p` asset; park on last frame (`parkVideoAtEnd`), `playOnce` per SPA session.

## Graceful degradation

- **`prefers-reduced-motion`**: cinema stage stays visible with `posterEnd` (last MP4 frame) via `posterOnly` — no video fetch or autoplay. **Desktop landscape:** sticky pin + Chi siamo card overlay top-right (`cinema-card--hold`), matching the scroll cinema end state. **Portrait:** Chi siamo below the short clip (`portraitMobile` only).
- **Portrait / narrow aspect** (`PORTRAIT_ASPECT_QUERY`): shorter pin (65svh), no scroll cinema; Chi siamo below the clip — orthogonal to reduced motion.
- **`play()` blocked** or session already spent: poster + play/replay control (`showAmbientControl`).
- Never block page content or navigation on video load; never autoplay with sound.

## When changing this

- Preserve degradation paths when adding polish (new animations, heavier assets, extra scroll logic).
- Do not add a second full-res source or autoplay multiple clips without measuring impact on slow connections.
- Keep logic in `ambient-video.ts` / `AmbientVideo.svelte`; keep cinema layout in `+page.svelte`.
- Update `ambient-video.test.ts` when session or control visibility rules change.
